Subject: [PATCH 415/488] [DS4.1] Adaptive verification's offsets in one
 TileLang kernel

reallocate_drafts launched five torch kernels for its offsets (two zeroes,
two add+cumsum pairs, the query_start_loc tail fill) plus a capacities
reset on a step without drafts. One block now scans both prefix sums in
shared memory, 256 requests a pass, writes the tail, and zeroes the
capacities when the step has no drafts. Tested bit for bit against the
torch chain across the scan's pass boundaries.
